{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC EVIDENCE, verified against merged main (Gerrit 2087, commit e92e3585dd).\n\nAC1 concern #12 heading present. AC2 all four checks over the #12 range: escape_input YES, shard YES, code-review-tests.md YES, and the no-duplication count returns 0. AC3 the portable core is COMPLETE - all seven checks pass against the patterns.md section ('can this assertion fail', escape_input, 'no finding without', fixture-mutates-foreign-state, mismatched-hardening-equivalence, unstated-policy-oracle, and the query line). AC4 all five schema fields present. AC5 'eleven concerns' returns 0 and 'twelve concerns' returns 1. AC6 verification.md carries both 'guarded production contract' and 'tree-state demonstration'. AC7 frontmatter names oracle strength and check_skill_frontmatter.py passes. AC9 the landed diff is exactly the five Scope files and nothing else; make lint and make typecheck (630 files) pass locally, and CI carried Verified +1 over the full suite.\n\nAC8 - the oracle CAN FAIL, proven by mutation rather than asserted. Editing discovery.md:181 from 'which of the twelve concerns above' to 'eleven' made test_schema_concern_count_matches_the_concern_list FAIL; restored, 3 passed. Fitting for a ticket about oracle strength that its own oracle was shown to bite rather than merely to pass.\n\nAC10 [operator-attested] - done DETERMINISTICALLY rather than as the stochastic janitor pass, and flagged as such so the record is not overstated. Transcript: the tree at 6fb4d801c9^ contains, in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_pandoc_emits_no_color_form, the assertion 'assert \"{color:\" not in completed.stdout' inside a loop that never inspects completed.returncode - unlike the test immediately above it, which does assert returncode == 0. CONCRETE escape_input: a pandoc child terminated by a signal before it writes (returncode -9, stdout ''). The substring test '\"{color:\" not in \"\"' is then trivially True, so the assertion passes while the property it claims to check was never exercised. That is the fail-OPEN absent-string oracle, and commit 6fb4d801c9 ('Stop absent-string child oracles failing open') fixed exactly it by adding assert_child_was_not_signal_killed(completed, what='pandoc'), whose own comment states the mechanism verbatim: 'a signal-killed pandoc is torn down before it writes, so \"{color:\" not in \"\" is trivially True'."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787391934226252001,"uuid":"b46f080b-bca5-4085-a50e-ba29e4a80c8c"}